From 013a10de807457aabf967107518d1137f51cec92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v <chickenhun@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:40:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(recursion): declare periodic columns in batch replay and
 interaction layouts

replay_batch_stark_transcript and RecursiveAir::declares_interactions
built their AirLayout without the AIR's periodic columns. For any batch
AIR with periodic columns the replay panicked in
AirLayout::validate_against_air ("num_periodic_columns does not match
AIR"), and declares_interactions evaluated the AIR with no periodic
values: an AIR indexing them panics, and one that tolerates their
absence can under-report its interactions to a check that decides
whether lookups are enforced. Both now declare num_periodic_columns,
as eval_folded_circuit and get_log_num_quotient_chunks already do.

Tests: a batch proof of an AIR gated by a periodic column replays; an
AIR whose bus interaction reads a periodic column is detected. Both
fail without the fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
